sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Returning Customer
    participant WA as Meta Cloud API
    participant CE as Conversation Engine
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    Note over C,DB: FR-08 — PLANNED, next after menu management. Design from August 2026.<br/>Open before its brief: which past order is "the usual" (most recent or most frequent),<br/>and the exact wording. Target: first message to confirmed order in under 30 seconds.
    C->>WA: first message
    WA->>CE: webhook (after the signature check and the dedup gate)
    CE->>DB: resolve restaurant · opening hours · open session (as built)
    CE->>DB: SELECT the customer's usual order at this restaurant<br/>(idx_orders_customer_completed)
    DB-->>CE: prior order + its items (order_items.menu_item_id)
    alt no prior completed order
        CE->>WA: welcome + full menu (as today)
    else prior order exists
        CE->>DB: check every item against today's menu: available, current price
        DB-->>CE: current availability and prices
        alt one or more items unavailable
            CE->>WA: welcome + "your usual is partly unavailable" + name the items
            Note over CE,WA: The suggestion is never shown with a stale price<br/>or an item the kitchen cannot make.
        else all items still available
            CE->>WA: welcome + "reorder your usual? [items, total]" + "or browse the menu"
        end
        alt customer accepts
            CE->>DB: pre-fill the cart with the same items at today's prices
            CE->>DB: CAS session to fulfillment_choice (or cart_review when pickup only)
            CE->>WA: pickup or delivery, then the summary, ready to confirm
            Note over C,DB: Browsing is skipped entirely — this is the<br/>whole point of the requirement.
        else customer browses instead
            CE->>WA: full menu
        end
    end
